  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "CHANGE OF USE OF&nbsp;DWELLINGHOUSE AND GARDEN\r\nOUTBUILDING TO FLEXIBLE USE CLASS C3/SUI GENERIS USE (MIXED RESIDENTIAL (USE CLASS C3)\r\nAND CHILDMINDING USE (USE CLASS E) TO ALLOW FOR A CHILDMINDING BUSINESS BETWEEN 8AM -&nbsp;5PM ON MONDAY - FRIDAY (MAXIMUM 8 CHILDREN).",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The development would result in the loss of a family sized unit thereby failing to comply with policy H11.1 of Merton Local Plan 2024.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a Fire Safety Strategy the scheme fails to address fire safety concerns and is therefore contrary to London Plan (2021) Policy D12.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By reason of absence of sufficient cycle and car parking facilities, the scheme impacts the free flow of traffic in the locality to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety and is contrary to, in particular, policy T16.2 of Merton&#x27;s Local Plan 2024 and T5 of the London Plan 2021.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The proposed use of the outbuilding and part main dwelling at 83 Belmont Avenue as a childminding operation by reason of is backland siting, intensification of use of the site results in an incongruous and unneighbourly form of development that fails to reflect the residential character of the locality to the detriment of the residential amenity of the adjacent residents in terms of noise and disturbance contrary to Policy D12.4 of Merton Local Plan (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
